[{:db/id "q-28655/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "a1470e22-19d9-5b99-b4aa-1e2119168a19" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-28655/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer/id #uuid "52a505e2-c0a0-5da5-a805-b4d632490090" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-28655/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer/id #uuid "ee7afe86-015e-5f44-b80a-651c68887da2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-28655/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "d9123221-05a5-5ca8-a2a4-3b151d06032a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-28655/selection/4de395131b8c6206950603752bf3404c42f4dd6f0a41fee38e42388d1b92c133" :answer/id #uuid "8d2cb22f-759e-5f66-a11b-d07d0cabc3ae" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-28655/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "f4da8a68-57fa-5444-88d2-e51880ea8d0e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-28655/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer-field/choices ["q-28655/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-28655/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" "q-28655/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" "q-28655/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" "q-28655/selection/4de395131b8c6206950603752bf3404c42f4dd6f0a41fee38e42388d1b92c133"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-28655" :question/id #uuid "19119cab-b147-5de2-999a-940899f58d4c" :question/math-academy-id "q-28655" :question/problem "Find ${h}^{′}(0)$ when $h(x)={5}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we express $h$ as the composite function\n\n$$\nh={5}^{u},\\,u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡v\\,v=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}h}{\\text{d}u}={5}^{u}\\operatorname{ln}⁡5,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}v}=\\frac{1}{v},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\n$$\n\nApplying now the chain rule twice, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}h}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}h}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}h}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}v}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={5}^{u}\\operatorname{ln}⁡5\\cdot (\\frac{1}{v})\\cdot (-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x) \\\\  & ={5}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\operatorname{ln}⁡5\\cdot (\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x})\\cdot (-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x) \\\\  & =-{5}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)}\\operatorname{ln}⁡5\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow we compute ${h}^{′}(0):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{h}^{′}(0) & =-{5}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{cos}⁡0)}\\operatorname{ln}⁡5\\operatorname{tan}⁡0 \\\\  & =-{5}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡1}\\operatorname{ln}⁡5(0) \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-28655/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f3ee0d5d-0821-5f6b-b613-6b814e65df50"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-28655"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-342927/field-1/34b4ec46bcf7424a4a188b820fb7f33a659fb79aa8e3196fc752b089c76bf903" :answer/id #uuid "5394d2d1-2862-54c9-bf13-ac330c8057ac" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\sin(2x-1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-342927/field-1/dadee93859d1569dc6e17be96443c18ed22cb7ce2370339a45d4991661f1a257" :answer/id #uuid "9cf509ac-948c-502e-925a-522182506b08" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sin(2x-1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-342927/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "af18e130-03b9-588e-ae2c-61e2f95a436b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-342927/field-1/34b4ec46bcf7424a4a188b820fb7f33a659fb79aa8e3196fc752b089c76bf903" :answer-field/choices ["q-342927/field-1/34b4ec46bcf7424a4a188b820fb7f33a659fb79aa8e3196fc752b089c76bf903" "q-342927/field-1/dadee93859d1569dc6e17be96443c18ed22cb7ce2370339a45d4991661f1a257"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-342927" :question/id #uuid "dabb04a7-0470-529a-9e2a-3b9e2c1be042" :question/math-academy-id "q-342927" :question/problem "Find ${y}^{′}$ when $y=\\sqrt{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x-1)}.$\n\n| ${y}^{′}$ | $=$ | {{field-1}} |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | $\\sqrt{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x-1)}$ |" :question/worked-solution "First, we express $y$ as the composite function\n\n$$\ny=\\sqrt{u},\\,u=\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,\\,v=2x-1.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}=\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{u}},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}v}=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=2.\n$$\n\nApplying now the chain rule twice, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}v}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{u}}\\cdot (-\\operatorname{sin}⁡v)\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x-1)}}\\cdot (-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x-1))\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =\\frac{-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x-1)}{2\\sqrt{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x-1)}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x-1)}{\\sqrt{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x-1)}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-342927/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f3ee0d5d-0821-5f6b-b613-6b814e65df50"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-342927"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-2397/selection/27a4757fbb7c1accd189b53d32032bd7a17d00ec6a4744f11a7285a4f1130a6a" :answer/id #uuid "0443124a-8281-51d1-b894-2ffd12c7720c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3x{sin}^{2}⁡(9{x}^{2}-1)\\,{cos}^{2}⁡(9{x}^{2}-1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-2397/selection/d3a6bbc4a7be4564675d7d29fe19813f3bcf91c9237b79d93aa0fa093134a711" :answer/id #uuid "a7aabba9-c859-551c-b1c1-66bb18472e21" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "18x{sin}^{2}⁡(9{x}^{2}-1)\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡(9{x}^{2}-1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-2397/selection/ec6d455d8be2bf73666312969b0e7902705aa4815991623ea786b3ce24771182" :answer/id #uuid "526e71e6-bf02-5b8d-8dad-6e915d6faad4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "54x{sin}^{2}⁡(9{x}^{2}-1)\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡(9{x}^{2}-1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-2397/selection/2ed6204f712a0df14e179e44e65c9198a1bff23c67c07f2d3ba207031b002c2f" :answer/id #uuid "a3983a1f-39c0-5fd8-a655-fc9c26a7b2d1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "54x{sin}^{3}⁡(9{x}^{2}-1)\\,{cos}^{3}⁡(9{x}^{2}-1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-2397/selection/01e0c7f42be92147a11404446d7603ed18f3c9b2f2009fbfe0c060b352baaa6f" :answer/id #uuid "2ee8b686-f04d-59d9-814b-0cff2488cc8a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "18x{sin}^{2}⁡(9{x}^{2}-1)\\,{cos}^{2}⁡(9{x}^{2}-1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-2397/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "022daecd-d7b4-5767-9457-1f7dac3ee10b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-2397/selection/ec6d455d8be2bf73666312969b0e7902705aa4815991623ea786b3ce24771182" :answer-field/choices ["q-2397/selection/27a4757fbb7c1accd189b53d32032bd7a17d00ec6a4744f11a7285a4f1130a6a" "q-2397/selection/d3a6bbc4a7be4564675d7d29fe19813f3bcf91c9237b79d93aa0fa093134a711" "q-2397/selection/ec6d455d8be2bf73666312969b0e7902705aa4815991623ea786b3ce24771182" "q-2397/selection/2ed6204f712a0df14e179e44e65c9198a1bff23c67c07f2d3ba207031b002c2f" "q-2397/selection/01e0c7f42be92147a11404446d7603ed18f3c9b2f2009fbfe0c060b352baaa6f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-2397" :question/id #uuid "2a7ed7da-3b96-5321-aaa3-c57d048a0cef" :question/math-academy-id "q-2397" :question/problem "Find ${f}^{′}(x)$ when $f(x)={sin}^{3}⁡(9{x}^{2}-1).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we express $f$ as the composite function\n\n$$\nf={u}^{3},\\,u=\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,\\,v=9{x}^{2}-1.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}=3{u}^{2},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}v}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=18x.\n$$\n\nApplying now the chain rule twice, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}v}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =3{u}^{2}\\cdot (\\operatorname{cos}⁡v)\\cdot 18x \\\\  & =3(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(9{x}^{2}-1))^{2}\\cdot (\\operatorname{cos}⁡(9{x}^{2}-1))\\cdot 18x \\\\  & =54x{sin}^{2}⁡(9{x}^{2}-1)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(9{x}^{2}-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-2397/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f3ee0d5d-0821-5f6b-b613-6b814e65df50"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-2397"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-31361/selection/7d2754c108cac43b4e89880212c4ba0cf03d6920f01407ea515ed0e041f6eb38" :answer/id #uuid "fd73b4ef-573a-5284-bb60-652c194d7c8b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "20\\operatorname{cot}⁡1{sec}^{2}⁡1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-31361/selection/9bef058f17607611c2af210386c233eeef190893c0426629783e01dd44bb4884" :answer/id #uuid "42d361d0-48da-55fe-86e7-357e129e89e3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "20{cot}^{3}⁡1{csc}^{2}⁡1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-31361/selection/38045f81e2597fb60408e776514e95bd4f037867dba3b170c27650d613e95cc6" :answer/id #uuid "6929b6fc-f997-55bb-b859-bdbf49ae687d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5{cot}^{3}⁡1{sec}^{2}⁡1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-31361/selection/6b50727a6665e0744c6b9cc3cc4aaacaca5e382b7c057651e84e33f50780df32" :answer/id #uuid "271ca77b-3cc4-5162-a309-7add8c31eae3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4{cot}^{3}⁡1{csc}^{2}⁡1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-31361/selection/ace596349eb4a10355c59d874fab082a83c9f9d859372877402f2c7e662efde7" :answer/id #uuid "85da8d42-3791-5323-9e6d-f68d3ff43689" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4{cot}^{2}⁡1{csc}^{2}⁡1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-31361/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "7bd56ad7-c1af-5c1d-ba9a-73dc89fe0447" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-31361/selection/9bef058f17607611c2af210386c233eeef190893c0426629783e01dd44bb4884" :answer-field/choices ["q-31361/selection/7d2754c108cac43b4e89880212c4ba0cf03d6920f01407ea515ed0e041f6eb38" "q-31361/selection/9bef058f17607611c2af210386c233eeef190893c0426629783e01dd44bb4884" "q-31361/selection/38045f81e2597fb60408e776514e95bd4f037867dba3b170c27650d613e95cc6" "q-31361/selection/6b50727a6665e0744c6b9cc3cc4aaacaca5e382b7c057651e84e33f50780df32" "q-31361/selection/ace596349eb4a10355c59d874fab082a83c9f9d859372877402f2c7e662efde7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-31361" :question/id #uuid "d323b0c1-7294-50f7-8607-7555968ab5bf" :question/math-academy-id "q-31361" :question/problem "Find ${f}^{′}(0)$ when $f(x)={cot}^{4}⁡(5x-1).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we express $f$ as the composite function\n\n$$\nf={u}^{4},\\,u=\\operatorname{cot}⁡v,\\,v=5x-1.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}=4{u}^{3},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}v}=-{csc}^{2}⁡v,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=5.\n$$\n\nApplying now the chain rule twice, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}v}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =4{u}^{3}\\cdot (-{csc}^{2}⁡v)\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =4(\\operatorname{cot}⁡(5x-1))^{3}\\cdot (-{csc}^{2}⁡(5x-1))\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =-20{cot}^{3}⁡(5x-1){csc}^{2}⁡(5x-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow we compute ${f}^{′}(0):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(0) & =-20{cot}^{3}⁡(5(0)-1){csc}^{2}⁡(5(0)-1) \\\\  & =-20{cot}^{3}⁡(-1){csc}^{2}⁡(-1) \\\\  & =-20(-{cot}^{3}⁡1){csc}^{2}⁡1 \\\\  & =20{cot}^{3}⁡1{csc}^{2}⁡1\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-31361/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f3ee0d5d-0821-5f6b-b613-6b814e65df50"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-31361"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-31352/selection/0b21347c8b91bbf7f164218fb476c0f34e6c3ea1c01ebe8c421d428f43fd5ea6" :answer/id #uuid "d0280610-74d3-5e76-afb5-570b31cd22c1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2(x+6)\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x+6)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-31352/selection/1c663237990469701aa775d82ff238806d27267efdb2bc8815a7fd8ed4b755b7" :answer/id #uuid "67f01430-60c9-577f-863c-f493f42cd459" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-{csc}^{2}⁡[(x+6)^{2}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-31352/selection/b7ea9032633182e903b0ceb6b7e2c01281cc9a9f180463d7f220350eadef09f8" :answer/id #uuid "c7d631a1-3d27-5d36-ade6-bd6af88af4e8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2x{csc}^{2}⁡[(x+6)^{2}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-31352/selection/1955745f9965cc96441813abba023449e43dcbb5fc44f0c974a4e07804158157" :answer/id #uuid "1ce87378-dd6f-5d41-9954-63bd96b1d88d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2(x+6){csc}^{2}⁡[(x+6)^{2}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-31352/selection/210f701289af5223e948331804e918472b1525e88136ab5f092fcb5a2d7c3061" :answer/id #uuid "cdf6d281-db07-5a56-b15f-1f7c9b361ac8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4(x+6)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-31352/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "8bfffeab-c1bb-5a99-8bc0-97e93b39a1b3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-31352/selection/1955745f9965cc96441813abba023449e43dcbb5fc44f0c974a4e07804158157" :answer-field/choices ["q-31352/selection/0b21347c8b91bbf7f164218fb476c0f34e6c3ea1c01ebe8c421d428f43fd5ea6" "q-31352/selection/1c663237990469701aa775d82ff238806d27267efdb2bc8815a7fd8ed4b755b7" "q-31352/selection/b7ea9032633182e903b0ceb6b7e2c01281cc9a9f180463d7f220350eadef09f8" "q-31352/selection/1955745f9965cc96441813abba023449e43dcbb5fc44f0c974a4e07804158157" "q-31352/selection/210f701289af5223e948331804e918472b1525e88136ab5f092fcb5a2d7c3061"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-31352" :question/id #uuid "ba826e94-e0a4-5375-be6a-13d761ae6472" :question/math-academy-id "q-31352" :question/problem "Find ${y}^{′}$ when $y=\\operatorname{cot}⁡[(x+6)^{2}].$" :question/worked-solution "First, we express $y$ as the composite function\n\n$$\ny=\\operatorname{cot}⁡u,\\,u={v}^{2},\\,v=x+6.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}=-{csc}^{2}⁡u,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}v}=2v,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=1.\n$$\n\nApplying now the chain rule twice, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}v}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =-{csc}^{2}⁡u\\cdot (2v)\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =-2(x+6){csc}^{2}⁡[(x+6)^{2}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-31352/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f3ee0d5d-0821-5f6b-b613-6b814e65df50"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-31352"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-9942/selection/624e12fec967b603c49e4b41010931fef672fd6a864713072b702efe71384f38" :answer/id #uuid "68be3b11-51d6-57ae-8518-06a2a6b17506" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x+2)+5x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x+2)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-9942/selection/8a57ef2cb9a8f9cc32967270a91950507224d6f964b34bd4356fd015b1d2bd0f" :answer/id #uuid "3870f6f5-4c57-5a21-b7d4-af0521206254" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x+2)+5{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x+2)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-9942/selection/e303b8f4999c6f03fd27c6466a25f1e8229620a9e228179635913f2e4dc791a3" :answer/id #uuid "e22e46fd-ce89-5b13-b282-ba9521c17cb5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x+2)+2{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x+2)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-9942/selection/0042f3c56d53c989605c435252370b5d02ce88d724c5733c327651fe73ed598b" :answer/id #uuid "8d72f78a-c78c-5ac0-86e9-dea6b39ff6aa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x+2)+{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x+2)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-9942/selection/7b9fba6a092e216e15f0cd5ca8780cc7631d6cc1260eae06bdaf5e29299234c6" :answer/id #uuid "6a92cbf4-de97-5ac8-89f6-99cdead0ac10" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x+2)+5{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x+2)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-9942/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "d1e3b272-65e1-5e06-b09c-f96760f72630" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-9942/selection/7b9fba6a092e216e15f0cd5ca8780cc7631d6cc1260eae06bdaf5e29299234c6" :answer-field/choices ["q-9942/selection/624e12fec967b603c49e4b41010931fef672fd6a864713072b702efe71384f38" "q-9942/selection/8a57ef2cb9a8f9cc32967270a91950507224d6f964b34bd4356fd015b1d2bd0f" "q-9942/selection/e303b8f4999c6f03fd27c6466a25f1e8229620a9e228179635913f2e4dc791a3" "q-9942/selection/0042f3c56d53c989605c435252370b5d02ce88d724c5733c327651fe73ed598b" "q-9942/selection/7b9fba6a092e216e15f0cd5ca8780cc7631d6cc1260eae06bdaf5e29299234c6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-9942" :question/id #uuid "ef4f244d-2de2-52d7-9bcd-09d23d44c0c4" :question/math-academy-id "q-9942" :question/problem "If $f(x)={x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x+2),$ find ${f}^{′}(x).$" :question/worked-solution "This question requires the product rule. Let $u(x)={x}^{2}$ and $v(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x+2).$ Then\n\n$$\n{u}^{′}(x)=2x,\\,{v}^{′}(x)=5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x+2).\n$$\n\nNote that we used the chain rule to differentiate $v.$\n\nNow, applying the product rule and simplifying, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}=\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & ={u}^{′}(x)\\cdot v(x)+u(x)\\cdot {v}^{′}(x) \\\\  & =(2x)(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x+2))+({x}^{2})(5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x+2)) \\\\  & =2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x+2)+5{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x+2).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-9942/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1c269944-636a-50f2-bfc9-c32a7b2e7ca3"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-9942"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-2392/selection/9b01527e27f38894bd68e0234868321bcf8a1da18bc9cc768839a7f154490fa6" :answer/id #uuid "875759ff-ea48-5385-ad0e-3d605905ea15" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3{sec}^{2}⁡x+3{a}^{3x}\\operatorname{tan}⁡x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-2392/selection/763d0c110d2590ea60bfb13ce8b7d26e54060939c9b898328f72a45577735590" :answer/id #uuid "71930411-4b10-53ef-95f7-2491fbb7401b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{a}^{3x}({sec}^{2}⁡x+3\\operatorname{tan}⁡x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-2392/selection/d68ef897ab9860f8d7fde7dc43fbcb1f377f29896b8c442378c42c9b1bc47156" :answer/id #uuid "ae968b51-4ba0-5eb1-ac0c-c3267ee5d579" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{a}^{3x}({sec}^{2}⁡x+3\\operatorname{ln}⁡a\\operatorname{tan}⁡x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-2392/selection/49c80d7c543b7df76c750fa9c9a9d23ff568018aa47dd7c414571fb048eafde3" :answer/id #uuid "4ca4322b-0aa8-589a-b696-325d8ce56f43" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3{a}^{3x}({sec}^{2}⁡x+\\operatorname{ln}⁡a\\operatorname{tan}⁡x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-2392/selection/1a18e269431be01b62df500aed800ae2dade57897735c564ab3b6db0ce650121" :answer/id #uuid "0e72bb9e-bf50-5f05-8fea-6643e8e5c873" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{a}^{3x}{sec}^{2}⁡x+3\\operatorname{tan}⁡x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-2392/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "6bb343fc-e533-5bb4-8af7-1e974f8437a0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-2392/selection/d68ef897ab9860f8d7fde7dc43fbcb1f377f29896b8c442378c42c9b1bc47156" :answer-field/choices ["q-2392/selection/9b01527e27f38894bd68e0234868321bcf8a1da18bc9cc768839a7f154490fa6" "q-2392/selection/763d0c110d2590ea60bfb13ce8b7d26e54060939c9b898328f72a45577735590" "q-2392/selection/d68ef897ab9860f8d7fde7dc43fbcb1f377f29896b8c442378c42c9b1bc47156" "q-2392/selection/49c80d7c543b7df76c750fa9c9a9d23ff568018aa47dd7c414571fb048eafde3" "q-2392/selection/1a18e269431be01b62df500aed800ae2dade57897735c564ab3b6db0ce650121"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-2392" :question/id #uuid "3cc0b95c-1856-5de2-836b-234ed6403eea" :question/math-academy-id "q-2392" :question/problem "Calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ for $y={a}^{3x}\\operatorname{tan}⁡x.$" :question/worked-solution "This question requires the product rule. Let $u(x)=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x$ and $v(x)={a}^{3x}.$ Then\n\n$$\n{u}^{′}(x)={sec}^{2}⁡x,\\,{v}^{′}(x)=3{a}^{3x}\\operatorname{ln}⁡a.\n$$\n\nNote that we used the chain rule to differentiate $v.$\n\nNow, applying the product rule and simplifying, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={u}^{′}(x)\\cdot v(x)+u(x)\\cdot {v}^{′}(x) \\\\  & =({sec}^{2}⁡x)({a}^{3x})+(\\operatorname{tan}⁡x)(3{a}^{3x}\\operatorname{ln}⁡a) \\\\  & ={a}^{3x}({sec}^{2}⁡x+3\\operatorname{ln}⁡a\\operatorname{tan}⁡x).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-2392/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1c269944-636a-50f2-bfc9-c32a7b2e7ca3"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-2392"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-10009/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "d67420c2-d9f9-5af0-8fa1-6c7483fbc14a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-10009/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "e379f4ed-96fc-54e8-8343-e7cc7dbd548b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-10009/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "2f09a3ed-5703-5d97-89c0-061a8ca7796a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-10009/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer/id #uuid "f3f0ffea-2d18-5020-a1b2-92d74de3da0a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-10009/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "e8067465-e26d-5981-81be-8eb81be4480d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-10009/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "6fd66f9f-c00b-54af-af6e-42d63823f63d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-10009/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer-field/choices ["q-10009/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-10009/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" "q-10009/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-10009/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" "q-10009/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-10009" :question/id #uuid "af401821-15de-511b-ae7d-83263ee65d61" :question/math-academy-id "q-10009" :question/problem "Find the slope of $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x$ at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the slope at a given point, we have to find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ at that point.\n\nThis question requires the product rule. Let $u(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x$ and $v(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x.$ Then\n\n$$\n{u}^{′}(x)=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x,\\,{v}^{′}(x)=-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x.\n$$\n\nNote that we used the chain rule to differentiate $u$ and $v.$\n\nNow, applying the product rule and simplifying, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={u}^{′}(x)\\cdot v(x)+u(x)\\cdot {v}^{′}(x) \\\\  & =(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x)(\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x)+(\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x)(-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x) \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x})|}_{x=\\pi /2} & =2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{2})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{2})-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{2})\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{2}) \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi )\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{2})-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi )\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{2}) \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-10009/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1c269944-636a-50f2-bfc9-c32a7b2e7ca3"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-10009"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-11824/selection/49e1d76c83e9333f0d7ed086871f6ddf3bbf01f60c872cffb97455356ece8a93" :answer/id #uuid "30de3564-36c3-5b89-a7d1-0ac882a7a75e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(9x+1){e}^{9x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11824/selection/05c5bf78a2f4a274c489d7906143149bf3f82de1e37d3d8766c35618bc388f68" :answer/id #uuid "ab3aa463-cd3f-5a68-8b33-e28f2c51b2a8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9x{e}^{9x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11824/selection/f68e91152a6bbf3a9e3337abe9be2048b54b8d0ea5c87ea47ab8a62d16e93eed" :answer/id #uuid "daf469be-b289-52dd-8823-1062d5390f95" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9(x+1){e}^{9x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11824/selection/11a2aec792a75aaa1977f93652316adf864223a1831a720bb2c4b041dfb3f498" :answer/id #uuid "39574bcf-9d44-56f9-89f4-8cb38b5f0839" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(9x+10){e}^{9x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11824/selection/f057b358a23decbd8461ac6a27c97acedc5322b103c06ef59362eea6f0217119" :answer/id #uuid "f8cc61d7-1d4e-550e-abaf-a727fc21ef7a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(x+1){e}^{9x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11824/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "b81c9e8f-3785-5c2e-a976-836a987cad2d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-11824/selection/11a2aec792a75aaa1977f93652316adf864223a1831a720bb2c4b041dfb3f498" :answer-field/choices ["q-11824/selection/49e1d76c83e9333f0d7ed086871f6ddf3bbf01f60c872cffb97455356ece8a93" "q-11824/selection/05c5bf78a2f4a274c489d7906143149bf3f82de1e37d3d8766c35618bc388f68" "q-11824/selection/f68e91152a6bbf3a9e3337abe9be2048b54b8d0ea5c87ea47ab8a62d16e93eed" "q-11824/selection/11a2aec792a75aaa1977f93652316adf864223a1831a720bb2c4b041dfb3f498" "q-11824/selection/f057b358a23decbd8461ac6a27c97acedc5322b103c06ef59362eea6f0217119"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-11824" :question/id #uuid "ac4f2143-0b5a-5a4d-94fb-d6c2015bc5dd" :question/math-academy-id "q-11824" :question/problem "Given that $y=(x+1){e}^{9x},$ find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.$" :question/worked-solution "This question requires the product rule. Let $u(x)=x+1$ and $v(x)={e}^{9x}.$ Then\n\n$$\n{u}^{′}(x)=1,\\,{v}^{′}(x)=9{e}^{9x}.\n$$\n\nNote that we used the chain rule to differentiate $v.$\n\nNow, applying the product rule and simplifying, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={u}^{′}(x)\\cdot v(x)+u(x)\\cdot {v}^{′}(x) \\\\  & =(1)({e}^{9x})+(x+1)(9{e}^{9x}) \\\\  & ={e}^{9x}+9(x+1){e}^{9x} \\\\  & =(1+9(x+1)){e}^{9x} \\\\  & =(9x+10){e}^{9x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-11824/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1c269944-636a-50f2-bfc9-c32a7b2e7ca3"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-11824"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-343332/field-1/17b151c4bf356febadc986f6e0ee321135ff3fc45a5d27099f8b2079838b5269" :answer/id #uuid "dd2c923a-3229-5cec-8fc8-f0110187612c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sin(4x)+4\\cos(4x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-343332/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "efc23796-5445-50a2-9807-f38542b4f6f2" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-343332/field-1/17b151c4bf356febadc986f6e0ee321135ff3fc45a5d27099f8b2079838b5269" :answer-field/choices ["q-343332/field-1/17b151c4bf356febadc986f6e0ee321135ff3fc45a5d27099f8b2079838b5269"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-343332" :question/id #uuid "9a7c912f-983c-5247-a010-73ac3f66fd43" :question/math-academy-id "q-343332" :question/problem "Calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ for $y={e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x.$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=($\n{{field-1}} $){e}^{x}$" :question/worked-solution "This question requires the product rule. Let $u(x)={e}^{x}$ and $v(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x.$ Then\n\n$$\n{u}^{′}(x)={e}^{x},\\,{v}^{′}(x)=4\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x.\n$$\n\nNote that we used the chain rule to differentiate $v.$\n\nNow, applying the product rule and simplifying, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={u}^{′}(x)\\cdot v(x)+u(x)\\cdot {v}^{′}(x) \\\\  & =({e}^{x})(\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x)+(4\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x)({e}^{x}) \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x+4\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x){e}^{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-343332/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1c269944-636a-50f2-bfc9-c32a7b2e7ca3"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-343332"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-343576/field-1/6f256a76ca0dd8a90a6af02e96766602f3d6fa4a1afbd96a088567cba97ae3c8" :answer/id #uuid "efb2187f-87ee-5a67-8776-3d0d640d6acf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{8e^3}{9}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-343576/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "af76b1f0-c145-5775-8da2-ee7237e43d48" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-343576/field-1/6f256a76ca0dd8a90a6af02e96766602f3d6fa4a1afbd96a088567cba97ae3c8" :answer-field/choices ["q-343576/field-1/6f256a76ca0dd8a90a6af02e96766602f3d6fa4a1afbd96a088567cba97ae3c8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-343576" :question/id #uuid "dc7457da-add5-5033-834e-3210499e9469" :question/math-academy-id "q-343576" :question/problem "If $y=\\frac{{e}^{3x}}{x+2},$ find ${y}^{′}(1).$\n\n${y}^{′}(1)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We use the quotient rule with the numerator $u(x)={e}^{3x}$ and the denominator $v(x)=x+2.$\n\nDifferentiating $u(x)$ and $v(x),$ we have\n\n$$\n{u}^{′}(x)=3{e}^{3x},\\,{v}^{′}(x)=1.\n$$\n\nNote that we used the chain rule to differentiate $u.$\n\nNow, applying the quotient rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{{u}^{′}(x)\\cdot v(x)-u(x)\\cdot {v}^{′}(x)}{[v(x)]^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(3{e}^{3x})(x+2)-{e}^{3x}(1)}{(x+2)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(3x+6-1)\\,{e}^{3x}}{(x+2)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(3x+5)\\,{e}^{3x}}{(x+2)^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the value of ${y}^{′}(x)$ at $x=1$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(1) & =\\frac{(3(1)+5)({e}^{3(1)})}{((1)+2)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{8{e}^{3}}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-343576/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "261910cd-a1a4-5c90-8caa-238208558458"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-343576"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-11973"] :question/worked-solution "We use the quotient rule with the numerator $u(x)=3{x}^{2}$ and the denominator $v(x)=(3x+5)^{2}.$ \n\nDifferentiating $u(x)$ and $v(x),$ we have\n\n$$\n{u}^{′}(x)=6x,\\,{v}^{′}(x)=6(3x+5).\n$$\n\nNote that we used the chain rule to differentiate $v.$\n\nNow, applying the quotient rule and simplifying, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{{u}^{′}(x)\\cdot v(x)-u(x)\\cdot {v}^{′}(x)}{[v(x)]^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(6x){(3x+5)}^{2}-(3{x}^{2})\\cdot 6(3x+5)}{{((3x+5)^{2})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{6x(3x+5)(3x+5-3x)}{{(3x+5)}^{4}} \\\\  & =\\frac{6x(3x+5)(5)}{{(3x+5)}^{4}} \\\\  & =\\frac{30x}{{(3x+5)}^{3}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-343546/field-1/b23450b5701f302918c95457e8c95b407881794fa6cf5ace5507aa6b295d8fc4" :answer/id #uuid "dcf55986-23c1-53f3-baf2-54dc3e95910e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{6}{\\pi}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-343546/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "69397bbd-19b2-59fc-8ad3-025cbb5c2afe" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-343546/field-1/b23450b5701f302918c95457e8c95b407881794fa6cf5ace5507aa6b295d8fc4" :answer-field/choices ["q-343546/field-1/b23450b5701f302918c95457e8c95b407881794fa6cf5ace5507aa6b295d8fc4"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-343546" :question/id #uuid "cfa96c3e-3660-5ea3-8618-6409b518e6bc" :question/math-academy-id "q-343546" :question/problem "Find the slope $m$ of the tangent line to the curve $f(x)=\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x}{x}$ at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}.$\n\n$m=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We use the quotient rule with the numerator $u(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)$ and the denominator $v(x)=x.$\n\nDifferentiating $u(x)$ and $v(x),$ we have\n\n$$\n{u}^{′}(x)=-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x),\\,{v}^{′}(x)=1.\n$$\n\nNote that we used the chain rule to differentiate $u.$\n\nNow, applying the quotient rule and simplifying, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{{u}^{′}(x)\\cdot v(x)-u(x)\\cdot {v}^{′}(x)}{[v(x)]^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x))(x)-(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x))(1)}{{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-3x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{{x}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & ={f}^{′}\\,(\\frac{\\pi }{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{-3(\\frac{\\pi }{2})sin\\,(\\frac{3\\pi }{2})-cos\\,(\\frac{3\\pi }{2})}{{(\\frac{\\pi }{2})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-3(\\frac{\\pi }{2})(-1)-0}{\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{4}} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{\\pi }.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-343546/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "261910cd-a1a4-5c90-8caa-238208558458"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-343546"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-11978/selection/fdee32dd6e5a0bdf9e822dab7c41ff4b0242a5cdc7cf9a95fa212d513d0ae991" :answer/id #uuid "447e4b73-1241-5aa4-b059-4f8b11f3010d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2(1-x)}{{({x}^{2}+1)}^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11978/selection/fdbf0c5cd2a9cb4ef3e39623db3022899206d71d5d1c041534eb6a05ad103cde" :answer/id #uuid "0d475a46-ac9e-5a93-a5f8-a773369ddfa7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2(x+1)}{{({x}^{2}+1)}^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11978/selection/fe91c869799141c6f7bad5499a8e5f4251c8c438c0e01f4de15543294962c770" :answer/id #uuid "80b1e053-447b-51ae-ad6d-1678ce0ad780" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{(1-x)^{2}}{{({x}^{2}+1)}^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11978/selection/997c9ff0d30538fb8458bb74a52d70cb2b63c780e25de5f74a626a2a578d3f51" :answer/id #uuid "350a83e0-7923-5b08-9392-87ad87b493ef" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2(1-{x}^{2})}{{({x}^{2}+1)}^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11978/selection/809791d8a8e0fb1b9d17908be9386d763a5ab0e26dee5c60ed4f8ff5298ebf4f" :answer/id #uuid "9edca068-3380-5f7b-8546-48890d080555" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{(1-2{x}^{2})}{{({x}^{2}+1)}^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11978/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "a69f7ba6-4320-560f-9024-6f57f32bc283" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-11978/selection/997c9ff0d30538fb8458bb74a52d70cb2b63c780e25de5f74a626a2a578d3f51" :answer-field/choices ["q-11978/selection/fdee32dd6e5a0bdf9e822dab7c41ff4b0242a5cdc7cf9a95fa212d513d0ae991" "q-11978/selection/fdbf0c5cd2a9cb4ef3e39623db3022899206d71d5d1c041534eb6a05ad103cde" "q-11978/selection/fe91c869799141c6f7bad5499a8e5f4251c8c438c0e01f4de15543294962c770" "q-11978/selection/997c9ff0d30538fb8458bb74a52d70cb2b63c780e25de5f74a626a2a578d3f51" "q-11978/selection/809791d8a8e0fb1b9d17908be9386d763a5ab0e26dee5c60ed4f8ff5298ebf4f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-11978" :question/id #uuid "92523772-6de5-5832-955f-4e96488833e4" :question/math-academy-id "q-11978" :question/problem "Given that $y=\\frac{(x+1)^{2}}{{x}^{2}+1},$ find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.$" :question/worked-solution "We use the quotient rule with the numerator $u(x)=(x+1)^{2}$ and the denominator $v(x)={x}^{2}+1.$ \n\nDifferentiating $u(x)$ and $v(x),$ we have\n\n$$\n{u}^{′}(x)=2(x+1),\\,{v}^{′}(x)=2x.\n$$\n\nNote that we used the chain rule to differentiate $u.$\n\nNow, applying the quotient rule and simplifying, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{{u}^{′}(x)\\cdot v(x)-u(x)\\cdot {v}^{′}(x)}{[v(x)]^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(2(x+1))({x}^{2}+1)-((x+1)^{2})(2x)}{({x}^{2}+1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2(x+1)({x}^{2}+1)-2x(x+1)^{2}}{({x}^{2}+1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2(x+1)(({x}^{2}+1)-x(x+1))}{({x}^{2}+1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2(x+1)({x}^{2}+1-{x}^{2}-x)}{({x}^{2}+1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2(x+1)(1-x)}{({x}^{2}+1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2(1-{x}^{2})}{({x}^{2}+1)^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-11978/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "261910cd-a1a4-5c90-8caa-238208558458"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-11978"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-2396"] :question/worked-solution "We use the quotient rule with the numerator $u(x)=\\operatorname{tan}⁡(7x-2)$ and the denominator $v(x)=4x.$ \n\nDifferentiating $u(x)$ and $v(x),$ we have\n\n$$\n{u}^{′}(x)=7{sec}^{2}⁡(7x-2),\\,{v}^{′}(x)=4.\n$$\n\nNote that we used the chain rule to differentiate $u.$\n\nNow, applying the quotient rule and simplifying, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}=\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{{u}^{′}(x)\\cdot v(x)-u(x)\\cdot {v}^{′}(x)}{[v(x)]^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(7{sec}^{2}⁡(7x-2))(4x)-\\operatorname{tan}⁡(7x-2)(4)}{(4x)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4(7x{sec}^{2}⁡(7x-2)-\\operatorname{tan}⁡(7x-2))}{16{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{⧸}4(7x{sec}^{2}⁡(7x-2)-\\operatorname{tan}⁡(7x-2))}{\\text{⧸}4(4{x}^{2})} \\\\  & =\\frac{7x{sec}^{2}⁡(7x-2)-\\operatorname{tan}⁡(7x-2)}{4{x}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
